  "notes": "GAAP audit, FYE 9/30/2023. Page 1 is an MD&A page (expenditures by function), not a schedule. Governmental lines from the Statement of Revenues, Expenditures, and Changes in Fund Balances, Total Governmental Funds column (pp6-7). Beginning fund balance as originally reported 33,452,767 with prior period adjustment (272,654) (note 13) recorded in adjustments; restated 33,180,113. SBITA 524,246 (other financing source) recorded as debt_proceeds. ending_cash = cash and cash equivalents + cash at county treasurer from the governmental funds Balance Sheet (p5); investments 17,085,684 in ending_investments; beginning cash not printed. Business-type from the proprietary statement, Total Enterprise Funds column (pp10-11); the Governmental Activities Internal Service Fund column is excluded (it belongs to governmental activities and is not in the governmental funds statements). Business-type receipts total = operating revenues 20,626,636 + investment earnings 967,468 (no single printed total); disbursements = operating expenses 11,039,499 + interest expense, net 874,848 + loss on disposal 969. Business-type beginning net position as previously stated 77,743,501, prior period adjustment 160,407, restated 77,903,908. Utility spending by cost type with function utilities. Proprietary cash flows from Total Enterprise Funds (pp12-13). Balance sheet = government-wide Statement of Net Position (p2) by activity column. Detail = the five budget-basis budget-to-actual schedules (General, Streets/Engineering, Sales Tax, 1/2 Cent Sales Tax, ARP Act; pp14-18); zero-actual 'Proceeds from long-term debt, net' lines (budget 4,300,000 General, 2,396,868 Streets) not recorded; no schedules for nonmajor or enterprise funds, so no statement lines added for them. Read pages 1-18 of 18"
}
